For this source request, the processor will insert the exact retained context
as the example text for each term's contextual sense. It will also copy the
matching translation from the root "source_context_translations" array. Follow
these rules:

1. Translate each object in the input "contexts" array exactly once, regardless
   of how many words refer to it. Return one object for every input context in
   the root "source_context_translations" array, with exactly these fields:
   "context_id" copied character-for-character from the input and
   "translation" containing one complete, natural English translation of the
   whole context. Do not add an unrequested context_id, omit a requested one,
   or return the same context_id twice.
2. Each context translation is one undelimited JSON string. It may contain
   normal English punctuation and multiple clauses or sentences, but never |
   or HTML. Do not split one context translation into
   several items. If the context is already Modern English, repeat it as plain
   text.
3. Keep the sense used in a term's retained source context as that term's first
   card entry. OMIT both "Sentences" and
   "Sentence Translations (English)" from this contextual entry. The processor
   supplies both values; do not repeat or rewrite the context or
   its translation inside the card. If the input word object supplies an
   "occurrence_span", that span identifies the exact occurrence whose sense
   this first entry must describe; do not use another identical spelling
   elsewhere in the retained context to select the sense.
4. For another genuinely disjoint common lexical sense, create a separate card
   entry as usual. It MUST include "Sentences" as exactly three array items and
   "Sentence Translations (English)" as exactly three positionally matched array
   items.

Only the first, contextual card entry for each supplied term may omit those two
sentence fields. Every additional sense entry must include both three-item
arrays. These source-context rules override any general example instruction
for contextual entries only.
